 ["In a chemical change a new substance forms and it cannot be changed back easily. Rusting, burning, cooking an egg and curdling milk are chemical changes.","In a physical change no new substance forms. Melting ice, dissolving sugar and cutting paper are physical changes.","Crystallisation is forming crystals from a solution when the water evaporates. It is a physical change."],
